WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
1968.

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.690
Medellín, Colombia.

3
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.420
Latin America's Catholic bishops meet.

4
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.970
Around them: deep poverty,
land and wealth held by a few,

5
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.190
and military dictatorships.

6
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.170
The bishops call this poverty
institutionalised violence.

7
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.820
In villages and slums, small
groups read the Bible together,

8
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.460
and ask what it says
about their own lives.

9
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.990
These priests said God
takes the side of the poor.

10
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.590
But what did they mean?

11
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.320
In this mission, you'll
meet Gustavo Gutiérrez,

12
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:35.080
the Peruvian priest who wrote
A Theology of Liberation.

13
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:40.160
Then you'll weigh up a hard question:
is it right to put one group first?

14
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:44.440
Your mission: find out what they meant
when they said God takes the side of the

15
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.170
poor.
